// sites.js — the 30 pieces of ground you can buy off the main map.
//
// GENERATED by tools/sites-bake.mjs — do not edit by hand, re-run the bake.
//
// The owner, 2026-10-21: "which side has the road so where the entrance is supposed to
// be… maybe the difference between plots of same kind is the side the entrance is off
// the road coming in." Every site here carries the side its road comes in from
// (roadSide), the bearing to that road (gateBearing), and — where two roads pass two
// edges — the corner pair the player chooses between (entranceSide).
//
// TWO TIERS (owner, 2026-10-21: "is there no really cheap shitty property? … otherwise
// you want a better one you must mortgage it"):
//   'good'  — 24 plots of workable ground, priced by plotmap.plotPrice (real Hogsback
//             comparables). H$120k-H$830k: a life buys these with a mortgage.
//   'rough' — 6 plots of steep, remote, dry ground growing nothing worth selling,
//             H$14k-H$42k. The ground nobody bid on, and the only land a life with
//             almost no money can own outright.
// Both tiers are bought on the same terms: 15% deposit, the rest over 8 years at the
// bank's rate (plotmap.LAND_MORTGAGE). The price is baked here so the picker, plot.html
// and the tests all read one number.
//
// The scan: the DEM for flat (or steep) ground, the real OSM roads for the entrance, the
// streams for water, the OSM stands for forest kind, the Hogsback village anchor for
// distance. Each site was then GENERATED and audited: ≥40 flat tiles in the clearing, a
// legal 4×3 camp site, and the gate on its declared road side. Names are measured, not
// invented: a summit is never "above" anything (see tools/sites-bake.mjs isSummit).
// Deterministic: same map, same 30 sites. The catalog is static — no runtime scan.

